cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ThoracicTCR in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ThoracicTCR: pan-thoracic TCR repertoire atlas and prognostic / ICI-response toolkit"
abstract: >-
  ThoracicTCR is an end-to-end pipeline and command-line toolkit that
  reconstructs T-cell receptor (TCR) repertoires from bulk RNA-Seq data
  across five thoracic cancers (LUAD, LUSC, ESCA, MESO, THYM), computes
  diversity / clonality / V-J usage / clone-size / motif metrics, builds
  a cross-cancer atlas, and ships with R/ggplot2 figure scripts for
  publication-ready outputs.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-27"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - T-cell receptor
  - TCR repertoire
  - bulk RNA-Seq
  - thoracic cancer
  - lung cancer
  - esophageal cancer
  - mesothelioma
  - thymoma
  - immune checkpoint inhibitor
  - diversity metrics
  - TRUST4
